# COS 201 Track B: Java OOP — Topic 2
# Classes, Objects, [[encapsulation|encapsulation]], Constructors

## The Central Idea

**Classes** are blueprints. **Objects** are instances. **[[encapsulation|encapsulation]]** hides internal [[state|state]] behind a [[public|public]] [[interface|interface]]. [[this|this]] topic covers the mechanics of defining classes, creating objects, controlling access, and initializing [[state|state]].

---

## Why It Matters — Past Exam Coverage

| Past Exam Question | [[this|this]] Topic Covers |
|--------------------|-------------------|
| "Explain how [[encapsulation|encapsulation]] is achieved in [[object|object]]-oriented programming, and write a program to support your explanation." | [[encapsulation|encapsulation]] + code |
| "Properties of Java Classes" | [[class|class]] structure |
| "Write a java program that creates a java [[class|class]] named 'Dog'..." | [[class|class]] definition, methods |
| "[[uml|uml]] to Java: User → Student/Lecturer/Admin" | [[class|class]] design |

---

## Section 1 — [[class|class]] Anatomy

### [[class|class]] Declaration
```java
[modifiers] [[class|class]] ClassName [[[extends|extends]] [[superclass|superclass]]] [[[implements|implements]] Interfaces] {
    // Fields (attributes/[[state|state]])
    // Constructors
    // Methods (behavior)
    // Nested classes
}
```

### Components

| [[component|component]] | Purpose | Example |
|-----------|---------|---------|
| **Fields** | [[state|state]] (data) | `[[private|private]] String name;` |
| **Constructors** | Initialize new objects | `[[public|public]] Dog(String name) { ... }` |
| **Methods** | Behavior | `[[public|public]] void bark() { ... }` |
| **Blocks** | Initialization code | `{ System.out.println("Loading..."); }` |

---

## Section 2 — Fields & [[encapsulation|encapsulation]]

### [[encapsulation|encapsulation]] Definition
> **Bundling data (fields) and methods that operate on that data within a single [[unit|unit]] ([[class|class]]), and restricting direct access to some of the [[object|object]]'s components.**

### Access Modifiers

| Modifier | [[class|class]] | Package | [[subclass|subclass]] | World |
|----------|-------|---------|----------|-------|
| `[[private|private]]` | ✓ | ✗ | ✗ | ✗ |
| (default) | ✓ | ✓ | ✗ | ✗ |
| `[[protected|protected]]` | ✓ | ✓ | ✓ | ✗ |
| `[[public|public]]` | ✓ | ✓ | ✓ | ✓ |

### [[encapsulation|encapsulation]] Pattern

```java
[[public|public]] [[class|class]] Student {
    // [[private|private]] fields — hidden from outside
    [[private|private]] String name;
    [[private|private]] int age;
    [[private|private]] double gpa;

    // [[public|public]] getters (read access)
    [[public|public]] String getName() { return name; }
    [[public|public]] int getAge() { return age; }
    [[public|public]] double getGpa() { return gpa; }

    // [[public|public]] setters (controlled write access)
    [[public|public]] void setName(String name) {
        if (name != null && !name.isBlank()) {
            [[this|this]].name = name;
        }
    }
    [[public|public]] void setAge(int age) {
        if (age >= 16 && age <= 100) {
            [[this|this]].age = age;
        }
    }
    [[public|public]] void setGpa(double gpa) {
        if (gpa >= 0.0 && gpa <= 5.0) {
            [[this|this]].gpa = gpa;
        }
    }
}
```

### Why [[encapsulation|encapsulation]]?
1. **Control** — validate before setting
2. **Flexibility** — change internal representation without breaking clients
3. **[[security|security]]** — prevent invalid [[state|state]]
4. **[[maintainability|maintainability]]** — single point of control

---

## Section 3 — Constructors

### Purpose
Initialize [[object|object]] [[state|state]] when `new` is called.

### Types

| Type | Syntax | When Called |
|--------|--------|-------------|
| **No-arg (default)** | `[[public|public]] Dog() { }` | `new Dog()` |
| **Parameterized** | `[[public|public]] Dog(String name) { ... }` | `new Dog("Rex")` |
| **Copy** | `[[public|public]] Dog(Dog other) { ... }` | `new Dog(existingDog)` |

### [[constructor|constructor]] Rules
- **Same name as [[class|class]]**
- **No return type** (not even `void`)
- **Can be overloaded** (different parameters)
- **If none defined**, Java provides default no-arg [[constructor|constructor]]
- **If ANY defined**, default is NOT provided

### `[[this|this]]()` — [[[[constructor|constructor]]-chaining|[[constructor|constructor]] chaining]]
```java
[[public|public]] [[class|class]] Dog {
    [[private|private]] String name;
    [[private|private]] int age;
    [[private|private]] String breed;

    [[public|public]] Dog() {
        [[this|this]]("Unknown", 0, "Mixed");  // Calls 3-arg [[constructor|constructor]]
    }

    [[public|public]] Dog(String name) {
        [[this|this]](name, 0, "Mixed");
    }

    [[public|public]] Dog(String name, int age, String breed) {
        [[this|this]].name = name;
        [[this|this]].age = age;
        [[this|this]].breed = breed;
    }
}
```

### `[[this|this]]` [[keyword|keyword]]
- `[[this|this]].[[field|field]]` — refers to [[instance-[[field|field]]|instance [[field|field]]]] (vs parameter)
- `[[this|this]]()` — calls another [[constructor|constructor]] (must be first line)
- `[[this|this]]` — reference to current [[object|object]]

---

## Section 4 — Methods

### [[method|method]] Signature
```java
[modifiers] returnType methodName(parameterList) [[[throws|throws]] Exceptions] {
    // body
    return value; // if not void
}
```

### [[[[method|method]]-overloading|[[method|method]] overloading]]
Same name, different parameter [[list|list]] (type, number, [[order|order]]).
```java
[[public|public]] void setName(String name) { ... }
[[public|public]] void setName(String first, String last) { ... }
```

### [[varargs|varargs]] ([[variable|variable]] Arguments)
```java
[[public|public]] void addScores(int... scores) {
    for (int s : scores) { total += s; }
}
// Call: addScores(80, 90, 85); or addScores(new int[]{80,90});
```

---

## Section 5 — Static Members

### Static Fields ([[class|class]] Variables)
- Shared by ALL instances
- One copy per [[class|class]], not per [[object|object]]
- Accessed via `ClassName.fieldName`

```java
[[public|public]] [[class|class]] Student {
    [[private|private]] static int studentCount = 0;  // [[class|class]] [[variable|variable]]
    [[private|private]] String name;                  // Instance [[variable|variable]]

    [[public|public]] Student(String name) {
        [[this|this]].name = name;
        studentCount++;  // Increment on each creation
    }

    [[public|public]] static int getStudentCount() {
        return studentCount;
    }
}

// Usage:
Student s1 = new Student("Alice");
Student s2 = new Student("Bob");
System.out.println(Student.getStudentCount());  // 2
```

### Static Methods
- Belong to [[class|class]], not instance
- **Cannot** use `[[this|this]]` or access instance members directly
- Utility methods, factories

```java
[[public|public]] [[class|class]] MathUtils {
    [[public|public]] static int max(int a, int b) {
        return (a > b) ? a : b;
    }
}
// Call: MathUtils.max(5, 10);
```

