# COS 201 Track B: Java OOP — Topic 3
# [[inheritance|inheritance]] & [[polymorphism|polymorphism]]

## The Central Idea

**[[inheritance|inheritance]]** lets a [[class|class]] acquire fields and methods from another [[class|class]] — "is-a" relationship. **[[polymorphism|polymorphism]]** lets objects of different types be treated uniformly through a common [[interface|interface]]. Together, they enable code reuse and flexible design.

---

## Why It Matters — Past Exam Coverage

| Past Exam Question | [[this|this]] Topic Covers |
|--------------------|-------------------|
| "Create a User base [[class|class]], and Create Student, Lecturer, and Admin classes that inherit from User base [[class|class]]. Demonstrate how an [[object|object]] of each derived [[class|class]] can use: Methods from the [[parent-[[class|class]]|parent [[class|class]]]], Its own specific methods." | [[inheritance|inheritance]], [[polymorphism|polymorphism]], [[[[method|method]]-overriding|[[method|method]] overriding]] |
| "With aid of diagram, [[list|list]] and explain the three types of [[class|class]] relationships in [[uml|uml]]" | [[uml|uml]] relationships ([[association|association]], [[aggregation|aggregation]], [[composition|composition]]) |

---

## Section 1 — [[inheritance|inheritance]] Basics

### Syntax
```java
[[class|class]] ChildClass [[extends|extends]] ParentClass {
    // Inherits all non-[[private|private]] members
    // Can add new fields/methods
    // Can override methods
}
```

### Key Points
- **[[single-[[inheritance|inheritance]]|single [[inheritance|inheritance]]]]** — Java: one parent only (`[[extends|extends]]` one [[class|class]])
- **`[[super|super]]` [[keyword|keyword]]** — access parent's members
- **Constructors not inherited** — but child [[constructor|constructor]] must call parent [[constructor|constructor]] (implicitly or explicitly)
- **`[[private|private]]` members** — not inherited (but exist in [[object|object]])

### Example: Base [[class|class]]
```java
[[public|public]] [[class|class]] User {
    // Common fields
    [[protected|protected]] String userId;
    [[protected|protected]] String name;
    [[protected|protected]] String email;

    [[public|public]] User(String userId, String name, String email) {
        [[this|this]].userId = userId;
        [[this|this]].name = name;
        [[this|this]].email = email;
    }

    // Common methods
    [[public|public]] void login() {
        System.out.println(name + " logged in.");
    }

    [[public|public]] void logout() {
        System.out.println(name + " logged out.");
    }

    [[public|public]] void displayInfo() {
        System.out.println("ID: " + userId + ", Name: " + name + ", Email: " + email);
    }
}
```

---

## Section 2 — Derived Classes (Student, Lecturer, Admin)

### Student
```java
[[public|public]] [[class|class]] Student [[extends|extends]] User {
    [[private|private]] String matricNumber;
    [[private|private]] String program;
    [[private|private]] int year;

    [[public|public]] Student(String userId, String name, String email, 
                   String matricNumber, String program, int year) {
        [[super|super]](userId, name, email);  // Call parent [[constructor|constructor]]
        [[this|this]].matricNumber = matricNumber;
        [[this|this]].program = program;
        [[this|this]].year = year;
    }

    // Student-specific methods
    [[public|public]] void registerCourse(String courseCode) {
        System.out.println(name + " registered for " + courseCode);
    }

    [[public|public]] void viewGrades() {
        System.out.println(name + " viewing grades...");
    }

    // Override parent [[method|method]]
    @Override
    [[public|public]] void displayInfo() {
        [[super|super]].displayInfo();  // Call parent version
        System.out.println("Matric: " + matricNumber + ", Program: " + program + ", Year: " + year);
    }
}
```

### Lecturer
```java
[[public|public]] [[class|class]] Lecturer [[extends|extends]] User {
    [[private|private]] String staffId;
    [[private|private]] String department;
    [[private|private]] String rank;  // e.g., "Assistant Professor"

    [[public|public]] Lecturer(String userId, String name, String email,
                    String staffId, String department, String rank) {
        [[super|super]](userId, name, email);
        [[this|this]].staffId = staffId;
        [[this|this]].department = department;
        [[this|this]].rank = rank;
    }

    // Lecturer-specific methods
    [[public|public]] void uploadMaterial(String courseCode, String material) {
        System.out.println(name + " uploaded material for " + courseCode);
    }

    [[public|public]] void gradeSubmission(String studentId, String assignment, double grade) {
        System.out.println(name + " graded " + assignment + " for " + studentId + ": " + grade);
    }

    @Override
    [[public|public]] void displayInfo() {
        [[super|super]].displayInfo();
        System.out.println("Staff ID: " + staffId + ", Dept: " + department + ", Rank: " + rank);
    }
}
```

### Admin
```java
[[public|public]] [[class|class]] Admin [[extends|extends]] User {
    [[private|private]] String adminId;
    [[private|private]] String role;  // e.g., "System Admin", "Registrar"
    [[private|private]] String[] permissions;

    [[public|public]] Admin(String userId, String name, String email,
                 String adminId, String role, String[] permissions) {
        [[super|super]](userId, name, email);
        [[this|this]].adminId = adminId;
        [[this|this]].role = role;
        [[this|this]].permissions = permissions;
    }

    // Admin-specific methods
    [[public|public]] void createUser(User user) {
        System.out.println(name + " created user: " + user.name);
    }

    [[public|public]] void generateReport(String reportType) {
        System.out.println(name + " generated " + reportType + " report");
    }

    @Override
    [[public|public]] void displayInfo() {
        [[super|super]].displayInfo();
        System.out.println("Admin ID: " + adminId + ", Role: " + role);
    }
}
```

