## Section 3 — [[polymorphism|polymorphism]]

### Definition
> **[[polymorphism|polymorphism]]** = "Many forms." A single [[interface|interface]], multiple implementations.

### Types

| Type | Mechanism | Example |
|------|-----------|---------|
| **Compile-time (Static)** | [[[[method|method]]-overloading|[[method|method]] overloading]] | `print(int)`, `print(String)` |
| **Runtime (Dynamic)** | [[[[method|method]]-overriding|[[method|method]] overriding]] | `user.displayInfo()` calls child's version |

### Runtime [[polymorphism|polymorphism]] Example

```java
[[public|public]] [[class|class]] TestInheritance {
    [[public|public]] static void main(String[] args) {
        // Create objects of each type
        User student = new Student("S001", "Alice", "alice@uni.edu", 
                                   "MAT2023", "Computer Science", 2);
        User lecturer = new Lecturer("L001", "Dr. Smith", "smith@uni.edu",
                                     "STF001", "Computer Science", "Senior Lecturer");
        User admin = new Admin("A001", "Admin User", "admin@uni.edu",
                               "ADM001", "Registrar", new String[]{"manage_users", "reports"});

        // Polymorphic array
        User[] users = {student, lecturer, admin};

        // Runtime [[polymorphism|polymorphism]]: calls overridden [[method|method]]
        for (User u : users) {
            u.displayInfo();  // Calls STUDENT's, LECTURER's, ADMIN's version
            u.login();        // Inherited from User
            System.out.println("---");
        }

        // [[downcasting|downcasting]] to access specific methods
        if (users[0] [[instanceof|instanceof]] Student) {
            Student s = (Student) users[0];
            s.registerCourse("CSC201");  // Student-specific
        }
    }
}
```

**[[output|output]]:**
```
ID: S001, Name: Alice, Email: alice@uni.edu
Matric: MAT2023, Program: Computer Science, Year: 2
Alice logged in.
---
ID: L001, Name: Dr. Smith, Email: smith@uni.edu
Staff ID: STF001, Dept: Computer Science, Rank: Senior Lecturer
Dr. Smith logged in.
---
ID: A001, Name: Admin User, Email: admin@uni.edu
Admin ID: ADM001, Role: Registrar
Admin User logged in.
---
Alice registered for CSC201
```

---

## Section 4 — [[[[method|method]]-overriding|[[method|method]] overriding]] Rules

| Rule | Description |
|------|-------------|
| **Same signature** | Same name, same parameter types |
| **Same return type** | Or covariant ([[subclass|subclass]] of parent's return) |
| **[[access-modifier|access modifier]]** | Cannot be more restrictive (`[[public|public]]` → `[[protected|protected]]` ✗) |
| **Exceptions** | Can [[throw|throw]] fewer/ narrower checked exceptions |
| **`[[final|final]]` methods** | Cannot be overridden |
| **`static` methods** | Hidden, not overridden |
| **`[[private|private]]` methods** | Not inherited, cannot be overridden |

### `@Override` Annotation
- **Optional but recommended**
- Compiler checks you're actually overriding
- Catches typos: `@Override [[public|public]] void displayinfo()` → error

---

## Section 5 — `[[super|super]]` [[keyword|keyword]]

| Usage | Example |
|-------|---------|
| **Call parent [[constructor|constructor]]** | `[[super|super]](userId, name, email);` |
| **Call parent [[method|method]]** | `[[super|super]].displayInfo();` |
| **Access parent [[field|field]]** | `[[super|super]].userId` (if hidden by child [[field|field]]) |

