## Section 6 — Abstract Classes & Methods

### [[abstract-[[class|class]]|abstract [[class|class]]]]
- Cannot be instantiated
- May have abstract methods (no body)
- Can have concrete methods

```java
[[public|public]] [[abstract-[[class|class]]|abstract [[class|class]]]] Shape {
    [[protected|protected]] String color;

    [[public|public]] Shape(String color) { [[this|this]].color = color; }

    // [[abstract-[[method|method]]|abstract [[method|method]]]] — MUST be implemented by [[subclass|subclass]]
    [[public|public]] abstract double area();

    // [[concrete-[[method|method]]|concrete [[method|method]]]] — inherited as-is
    [[public|public]] String getColor() { return color; }
}

[[public|public]] [[class|class]] Circle [[extends|extends]] Shape {
    [[private|private]] double radius;

    [[public|public]] Circle(String color, double radius) {
        [[super|super]](color);
        [[this|this]].radius = radius;
    }

    @Override
    [[public|public]] double area() {
        return Math.PI * radius * radius;
    }
}
```

---

## Section 7 — `[[final|final]]` [[keyword|keyword]]

| Applied To | Effect |
|------------|--------|
| **[[variable|variable]]** | Constant (assign once) |
| **[[method|method]]** | Cannot be overridden |
| **[[class|class]]** | Cannot be extended |

```java
[[public|public]] [[class|class]] Constants {
    [[public|public]] static [[final|final]] double PI = 3.14159;  // Constant
}

[[public|public]] [[class|class]] [[security|security]] {
    [[public|public]] [[final|final]] void encrypt() { ... }  // Cannot override
}

[[public|public]] [[[[final|final]]-[[class|class]]|[[final|final]] [[class|class]]]] Immutable {  // Cannot extend
    [[private|private]] [[final|final]] String value;
    [[public|public]] Immutable(String v) { [[this|this]].value = v; }
}
```

