## Section 9 — Self-Check Questions

1. Can a [[class|class]] extend multiple classes in Java?
2. What does `[[super|super]]()` do in a [[constructor|constructor]]?
3. Can you override a `[[private|private]]` [[method|method]]?
4. Can you override a `static` [[method|method]]?
5. What is dynamic [[method|method]] dispatch?
6. Can an [[abstract-[[class|class]]|abstract [[class|class]]]] have a [[constructor|constructor]]?
7. What happens if you don't implement an [[abstract-[[method|method]]|abstract [[method|method]]]]?

---

## Solutions

1. No — [[single-[[inheritance|inheritance]]|single [[inheritance|inheritance]]]] only (but can implement multiple interfaces)
2. Calls parent [[constructor|constructor]] (must be first line)
3. No — not inherited
4. No — static methods are hidden, not overridden
5. JVM determines actual [[method|method]] at runtime based on [[object|object]] type
6. Yes — called by [[subclass|subclass]] constructors via `[[super|super]]()`
7. Compiler error — [[class|class]] must also be abstract

