# COS 201 Track B: Java OOP — Topic 4
# [[aggregation|aggregation]] vs [[composition|composition]] in Code

## The Central Idea

**[[aggregation|aggregation]]** and **[[composition|composition]]** are both "has-a" relationships, but differ in **ownership** and **lifetime [[dependency|dependency]]**. [[this|this]] topic shows the exact code patterns [[for-each|for each]], matching the exam requirement to distinguish them with diagrammatic examples.

---

## Why It Matters — Past Exam Coverage

| Past Exam Question | [[this|this]] Topic Covers |
|--------------------|-------------------|
| "With aid of diagrammatic example, distinguish between [[aggregation|aggregation]] and [[composition|composition]]." | Code + [[uml|uml]] for both |

---

## Section 1 — Core Difference

| Aspect | [[aggregation|aggregation]] | [[composition|composition]] |
|--------|-------------|-------------|
| **Relationship** | Weak "has-a" | Strong "has-a" |
| **Ownership** | Shared | Exclusive |
| **Lifetime** | Independent | Dependent |
| **[[uml|uml]]** | [[hollow-diamond|hollow diamond]] (◇) | [[filled-diamond|filled diamond]] (◆) |
| **Code** | Part passed in / created elsewhere | Part created in [[constructor|constructor]] |

---

## Section 2 — [[aggregation|aggregation]] Code Pattern

### Characteristics
- Part exists **independently** of whole
- Part can belong to **multiple wholes**
- Whole **does not create** part
- Part passed via **[[constructor|constructor]]/[[setter|setter]]**

### Code Example: Department & Professor

```java
// Part: Exists independently
[[public|public]] [[class|class]] Professor {
    [[private|private]] String id;
    [[private|private]] String name;
    [[private|private]] String email;

    [[public|public]] Professor(String id, String name, String email) {
        [[this|this]].id = id;
        [[this|this]].name = name;
        [[this|this]].email = email;
    }

    [[public|public]] String getName() { return name; }
    // ... getters/setters
}

// Whole: Aggregates professors
[[public|public]] [[class|class]] Department {
    [[private|private]] String name;
    [[private|private]] [[list|list]]<Professor> professors;  // [[aggregation|aggregation]]

    [[public|public]] Department(String name) {
        [[this|this]].name = name;
        [[this|this]].professors = new [[arraylist|arraylist]]<>();
    }

    // Professor created OUTSIDE, passed in
    [[public|public]] void addProfessor(Professor prof) {
        professors.add(prof);
    }

    [[public|public]] void removeProfessor(Professor prof) {
        professors.remove(prof);
    }

    [[public|public]] void listProfessors() {
        System.out.println("Department: " + name);
        for (Professor p : professors) {
            System.out.println("  - " + p.getName());
        }
    }
}

// Usage: Professor exists independently
Professor prof1 = new Professor("P001", "Dr. Smith", "smith@uni.edu");
Professor prof2 = new Professor("P002", "Dr. Jones", "jones@uni.edu");

Department cs = new Department("Computer Science");
Department math = new Department("Mathematics");

// Same professor can belong to MULTIPLE departments
cs.addProfessor(prof1);
math.addProfessor(prof1);  // Shared!

cs.addProfessor(prof2);

// Deleting department does NOT delete professors
// prof1 and prof2 still exist
```

### [[uml|uml]] for [[aggregation|aggregation]]
```
┌──────────────┐       ◇──────────►┌─────────────┐
│  Department  │                   │  Professor  │
└──────────────┘  [[has-a|has a]] (weak)     └─────────────┘
```

---

## Section 3 — [[composition|composition]] Code Pattern

### Characteristics
- Part **cannot exist** without whole
- Part belongs to **exactly one whole**
- Whole **creates** part in [[constructor|constructor]]
- Part **destroyed** when whole is destroyed

### Code Example: House & Room

```java
// Part: Cannot exist without House
[[public|public]] [[class|class]] Room {
    [[private|private]] String name;
    [[private|private]] double area;  // sq meters
    [[private|private]] House house;  // Back-reference (optional)

    // Room created BY House, not externally
    Room(String name, double area, House house) {
        [[this|this]].name = name;
        [[this|this]].area = area;
        [[this|this]].house = house;
    }

    [[public|public]] String getName() { return name; }
    [[public|public]] double getArea() { return area; }
}

// Whole: Composes rooms
[[public|public]] [[class|class]] House {
    [[private|private]] String address;
    [[private|private]] [[list|list]]<Room> rooms;  // [[composition|composition]]

    [[public|public]] House(String address) {
        [[this|this]].address = address;
        [[this|this]].rooms = new [[arraylist|arraylist]]<>();
        // House CREATES its rooms
        rooms.add(new Room("Living Room", 25.0, [[this|this]]));
        rooms.add(new Room("Kitchen", 15.0, [[this|this]]));
        rooms.add(new Room("Bedroom 1", 20.0, [[this|this]]));
        rooms.add(new Room("Bedroom 2", 18.0, [[this|this]]));
        rooms.add(new Room("Bathroom", 8.0, [[this|this]]));
    }

    // No [[public|public]] addRoom — rooms created internally
    // (or [[private|private]] [[method|method]] for extensibility)

    [[public|public]] double totalArea() {
        double total = 0;
        for (Room r : rooms) {
            total += r.getArea();
        }
        return total;
    }

    [[public|public]] void listRooms() {
        System.out.println("House at " + address);
        for (Room r : rooms) {
            System.out.println("  - " + r.getName() + ": " + r.getArea() + " sqm");
        }
    }
}

// Usage
House myHouse = new House("123 University Ave");
myHouse.listRooms();
System.out.println("Total area: " + myHouse.totalArea() + " sqm");

// When myHouse is garbage collected, all Rooms are too
// Rooms cannot exist without a House
// Rooms cannot be shared between houses
```

### [[uml|uml]] for [[composition|composition]]
```
┌─────────┐       ◆──────────►┌─────────┐
│  House  │                   │  Room   │
└─────────┘  [[has-a|has a]] (strong)   └─────────┘
```

---

## Section 4 — Quick Comparison Code

### [[aggregation|aggregation]] (Shared, Independent)
```java
// Part
[[public|public]] [[class|class]] Engine {
    [[private|private]] String serialNumber;
    [[public|public]] Engine(String sn) { [[this|this]].serialNumber = sn; }
    [[public|public]] void start() { System.out.println("Engine " + serialNumber + " started"); }
}

// Whole
[[public|public]] [[class|class]] Car {
    [[private|private]] Engine engine;  // [[aggregation|aggregation]]

    [[public|public]] Car(Engine engine) {  // Engine passed in
        [[this|this]].engine = engine;
    }

    [[public|public]] void start() { engine.start(); }
}

// Usage
Engine v8 = new Engine("V8-001");
Car car1 = new Car(v8);
Car car2 = new Car(v8);  // Same engine in two cars!
v8.start();  // Works independently
```

### [[composition|composition]] (Exclusive, Dependent)
```java
// Part
[[public|public]] [[class|class]] Heart {
    [[private|private]] int beatsPerMinute;
    Heart() { [[this|this]].beatsPerMinute = 70; }
    [[public|public]] void beat() { System.out.println("Heart beating: " + beatsPerMinute + " bpm"); }
}

// Whole
[[public|public]] [[class|class]] Human {
    [[private|private]] Heart heart;  // [[composition|composition]]

    [[public|public]] Human() {
        [[this|this]].heart = new Heart();  // Human CREATES heart
    }

    [[public|public]] void live() { heart.beat(); }
}

// Usage
Human person = new Human();
person.live();  // Heart beats
// Heart cannot exist without Human
// Heart cannot be transplanted to another Human in [[this|this]] model
```

---

## Section 5 — Decision Guide

| Question | [[aggregation|aggregation]] | [[composition|composition]] |
|----------|-------------|-------------|
| Can part exist without whole? | Yes | No |
| Can part belong to multiple wholes? | Yes | No |
| Who creates the part? | External code | Whole's [[constructor|constructor]] |
| Should deleting whole delete part? | No | Yes |
| Is part shared? | Often | Never |

