# COS 201 Track B: Java OOP — Topic 5
# [[exception|exception]] Handling

## The Central Idea

**Exceptions** are objects representing errors or exceptional conditions. Java's [[exception|exception]] handling mechanism (`try-catch-[[finally|finally]]`, `[[throw|throw]]`, `[[throws|throws]]`) lets you separate error-handling code from normal logic, making programs more robust and maintainable.

---

## Why It Matters — Past Exam Coverage

| Past Exam Question | [[this|this]] Topic Covers |
|--------------------|-------------------|
| "[[exception|exception]] Handling: try/catch/[[finally|finally]], [[throws|throws]], custom exceptions" | Core Java [[exception|exception]] handling |

---

## Section 1 — [[[[exception|exception]]-hierarchy|[[exception|exception]] hierarchy]]

```
java.lang.Throwable
├── java.lang.Error (Unchecked) — Serious, usually unrecoverable
│   ├── OutOfMemoryError
│   ├── StackOverflowError
│   └── ...
└── java.lang.[[exception|exception]]
    ├── java.lang.RuntimeException (Unchecked) — Programming errors
    │   ├── NullPointerException
    │   ├── ArrayIndexOutOfBoundsException
    │   ├── IllegalArgumentException
    │   ├── ArithmeticException
    │   └── ...
    └── Checked Exceptions — Must be caught or declared
        ├── IOException
        ├── FileNotFoundException
        ├── SQLException
        ├── ClassNotFoundException
        └── ...
```

**Key Distinction:**
- **Checked** — Compiler enforces handling (catch or [[throws|throws]]). [[extends|extends]] `[[exception|exception]]` but not `RuntimeException`.
- **Unchecked** — Compiler doesn't enforce. [[extends|extends]] `RuntimeException` or `Error`.

---

## Section 2 — try-catch-[[finally|finally]]

### Syntax
```java
try {
    // Risky code
} catch (ExceptionType1 e) {
    // Handle ExceptionType1
} catch (ExceptionType2 e) {
    // Handle ExceptionType2
} [[finally|finally]] {
    // Always executes (cleanup)
}
```

### Rules
- **At least one** `catch` or `[[finally|finally]]` required
- `catch` blocks ordered **specific → general**
- `[[finally|finally]]` runs **always** (even with `return` in try/catch)
- `[[finally|finally]]` **does not run** if `System.exit()` called

### Example
```java
[[public|public]] double divide(double a, double b) {
    try {
        if (b == 0) {
            [[throw|throw]] new ArithmeticException("Division by zero");
        }
        return a / b;
    } catch (ArithmeticException e) {
        System.err.println("Error: " + e.getMessage());
        return Double.NaN;
    } [[finally|finally]] {
        System.out.println("Division [[operation|operation]] completed");
    }
}
```

---

## Section 3 — [[throws|throws]] Clause

### Purpose
Declare that a [[method|method]] **may [[throw|throw]]** checked exceptions. Caller must handle.

```java
[[public|public]] void readFile(String [[path|path]]) [[throws|throws]] IOException, FileNotFoundException {
    [[filereader|filereader]] [[reader|reader]] = new [[filereader|filereader]]([[path|path]]);
    // ... read
    [[reader|reader]].close();
}
```

### Rules
- **Checked exceptions** must be caught or declared
- **Unchecked** (`RuntimeException`, `Error`) optional
- Overriding [[method|method]]: can [[throw|throw]] **same or narrower** checked exceptions

---

## Section 4 — [[throw|throw]] Statement

### Explicitly [[throw|throw]] [[exception|exception]]
```java
[[public|public]] void setAge(int age) {
    if (age < 0 || age > 150) {
        [[throw|throw]] new IllegalArgumentException("Invalid age: " + age);
    }
    [[this|this]].age = age;
}
```

### Re-throwing
```java
try {
    // ...
} catch (IOException e) {
    // Log, then re-[[throw|throw]]
    [[throw|throw]] new RuntimeException("[[file|file]] error", e);  // Wrap
    // OR: [[throw|throw]] e;  // Re-[[throw|throw]] same
}
```

---

## Section 5 — try-with-resources (Java 7+)

### Auto-close Resources
```java
// Before: manual close in [[finally|finally]]
[[filereader|filereader]] [[reader|reader]] = null;
try {
    [[reader|reader]] = new [[filereader|filereader]]("[[file|file]].txt");
    // read
} [[finally|finally]] {
    if ([[reader|reader]] != null) [[reader|reader]].close();
}

// After: try-with-resources ([[autocloseable|autocloseable]])
try ([[filereader|filereader]] [[reader|reader]] = new [[filereader|filereader]]("[[file|file]].txt");
     [[bufferedreader|bufferedreader]] br = new [[bufferedreader|bufferedreader]]([[reader|reader]])) {
    String line = br.readLine();
    // ...
} // Auto-closed!
```

### Multiple Resources
```java
try (Connection conn = DriverManager.getConnection(url);
     Statement stmt = conn.createStatement();
     ResultSet rs = stmt.executeQuery(sql)) {
    // use resources
} // Closed in reverse [[order|order]]
```

---

## Section 6 — Custom Exceptions

### Checked [[custom-[[exception|exception]]|custom [[exception|exception]]]]
```java
[[public|public]] [[class|class]] InsufficientFundsException [[extends|extends]] [[exception|exception]] {
    [[private|private]] double balance;
    [[private|private]] double requested;

    [[public|public]] InsufficientFundsException(String message, double balance, double requested) {
        [[super|super]](message);
        [[this|this]].balance = balance;
        [[this|this]].requested = requested;
    }

    [[public|public]] double getBalance() { return balance; }
    [[public|public]] double getRequested() { return requested; }
}
```

### Unchecked [[custom-[[exception|exception]]|custom [[exception|exception]]]]
```java
[[public|public]] [[class|class]] InvalidTransactionException [[extends|extends]] RuntimeException {
    [[public|public]] InvalidTransactionException(String message) {
        [[super|super]](message);
    }

    [[public|public]] InvalidTransactionException(String message, Throwable cause) {
        [[super|super]](message, cause);
    }
}
```

### Usage
```java
[[public|public]] void withdraw(double amount) [[throws|throws]] InsufficientFundsException {
    if (amount > balance) {
        [[throw|throw]] new InsufficientFundsException(
            "Cannot withdraw " + amount, balance, amount);
    }
    balance -= amount;
}
```

