## Section 1 — Collections Hierarchy

```
java.util.[[collection|collection]] ([[interface|interface]])
├── [[list|list]] (ordered, duplicates allowed)
│   ├── [[arraylist|arraylist]] (dynamic array, fast random access)
│   ├── [[linkedlist|linkedlist]] (doubly-linked, fast insert/delete)
│   └── Vector (synchronized, legacy)
├── [[set|set]] (no duplicates)
│   ├── [[hashset|hashset]] (hash table, no [[order|order]])
│   ├── [[linkedhashset|linkedhashset]] (insertion [[order|order]])
│   └── [[treeset|treeset]] (sorted, Red-Black [[tree|tree]])
└── [[queue|queue]] (FIFO/ordered)
    ├── PriorityQueue (heap, priority [[order|order]])
    ├── ArrayDeque (double-ended [[queue|queue]])
    └── [[linkedlist|linkedlist]] (also [[implements|implements]] [[queue|queue]])

[[map|map]] ([[interface|interface]]) — not a [[collection|collection]]
├── [[hashmap|hashmap]] (hash table, no [[order|order]])
├── [[linkedhashmap|linkedhashmap]] (insertion [[order|order]])
├── [[treemap|treemap]] (sorted keys)
├── Hashtable (synchronized, legacy)
└── Properties (String key/value, legacy)
```

---

## Section 2 — [[list|list]]

### [[arraylist|arraylist]] vs [[linkedlist|linkedlist]]
| [[operation|operation]] | [[arraylist|arraylist]] | [[linkedlist|linkedlist]] |
|-----------|-----------|------------|
| `get(index)` | O(1) | O(n) |
| `add/remove end` | O(1)* | O(1) |
| `add/remove middle` | O(n) | O(1)† |
| Memory | Less overhead | More (node objects) |

*Amortized. †If you have the node reference.

### Common Operations
```java
[[list|list]]<String> names = new [[arraylist|arraylist]]<>();
names.add("Alice");           // Add to end
names.add(0, "Bob");          // Insert at index
names.get(1);                 // Access
names.[[set|set]](1, "Charlie");      // Replace
names.remove(0);              // Remove by index
names.remove("Bob");          // Remove by [[object|object]]
names.size();                 // Count
names.contains("Alice");      // Search
names.isEmpty();
names.clear();
```

---

