## Section 5 — [[generics|generics]]

### Why [[generics|generics]]?
- **[[type-safety|type safety]]** — compile-time checking
- **No casts** — cleaner code
- **[[reusability|reusability]]** — one [[class|class]], many types

### [[generic-[[class|class]]|generic [[class|class]]]]
```java
[[public|public]] [[class|class]] Box<T> {
    [[private|private]] T content;

    [[public|public]] void [[set|set]](T item) { content = item; }
    [[public|public]] T get() { return content; }
}

// Usage
Box<String> stringBox = new Box<>();
stringBox.[[set|set]]("Hello");
String s = stringBox.get();  // No [[cast|cast]] needed

Box<Integer> intBox = new Box<>();
intBox.[[set|set]](42);
```

### [[generic-[[method|method]]|generic [[method|method]]]]
```java
[[public|public]] <T> void printArray(T[] array) {
    for (T item : array) {
        System.out.println(item);
    }
}

// Usage
printArray(new String[]{"A", "B"});
